          "title": "You'll want to know: ревность",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ревность (révnost) — \"jealousy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Из-за ревности они часто ссорятся. Iz-za révnosti oní chásto ssóryatsya. They often quarrel because of jealousy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine; no plural in everyday use."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ревность (révnost) is a noun in -ость on the stem ревн-, which it shares with ревновать (revnovát) and ревнивый (revnívyy); EtymDB links it to Church Slavonic rĭvenie 'strife, quarrel'. An older sense, 'zeal', is still met in bookish Russian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
