          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "зависть (závist) — \"envy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Коллеги говорили о его успехе без зависти. Kollégi govoríli o yegó uspékhe bez závisti. His colleagues talked about his success without envy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. С завистью — enviously."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "зависть (závist) is built on за- and the root of видеть 'to see', so envy is a way of looking at what another person has; видеть is inherited from Proto-Slavic viděti, from PIE weyd- 'to see, to know' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
